{"type":"system","subtype":"task_started","task_id":"a6344cb48ea88ebbb","tool_use_id":"toolu_01FXrjvQWSFc6K3k2oYyLyeD","description":"R1: Methods + Experiments review","task_type":"local_agent","prompt":"You are Reviewer R1 for a top ML venue review (acceptance rate ~25%, 6-point scale: 1=Strong Reject, 6=Strong Accept). Your focus: **Methods and Experiments**.\n\n## Paper Summary\n\nTitle: \"When Does Temporal Abstraction Fail in World-Model RL? Reward Landscape Geometry Determines Conditioning-Induced Value Overestimation\"\n\nThe paper investigates Conditioning-Induced Value Overestimation (CIVO) — a failure mode in world-model RL where trained temporal embeddings (Δt-conditioning) amplify RSSM prediction errors into pathological critic overestimation. Through cross-environment experiments on DreamerV3 with Walker Walk, Cheetah Run, Cartpole Swingup, and Hopper Hop, the paper finds CIVO requires specific task properties: (1) nonlinear reward functions (reward gap > 2×), (2) high-dimensional observations for embedding gradient amplification, (3) smooth reward landscapes. Walker Walk is the only environment where CIVO manifests (NVE peak 2.59×, 100% pathological overestimation, 50% collapse). The NVE>1.5× diagnostic achieves AUROC 1.0 within Walker but degrades to 0.58 cross-environment. The paper positions itself as a \"cautionary tale\" about benchmark-specific findings in MBRL.\n\n## Key Tables and Results\n\n**Walker Walk (CIVO manifests):**\n- Trained dt-emb (008d): 3 seeds, all NVE > 1.5×, 50% collapse (seed 0: NVE 4.12, collapsed; seed 1: NVE 1.73, collapsed; seed 2: NVE 2.05, recovered)\n- dt_embed_dim=0 (008f): 2 seeds, no NVE > 1.5× (NVE 1.02, 1.26), but seed 1 declines to eval 148\n- Untrained dt-emb (008a): 3 seeds, all NVE < 1.0× (0.59-0.72), eval 550-778 (15-40% below baseline)\n- dt=1 imagination (008e_v3): 4 seeds, 50% collapse rate identical to dt=2, two pathways (A: classic CIVO, B: eval-driven instability)\n- Frozen dt-emb: NVE 0.47, eval 204 (22% baseline), gradient starvation\n- Full-SGS: NVE 0.55, eval 160, gradient starvation\n- Reward-only SGS: no-op, NVE 10.42, collapsed\n\n**Cheetah Run (no CIVO):**\n- Baseline: mean eval 663, CV 10%\n- Trained dt-emb: NVE peak 0.95-1.28, mean eval 570, -12% vs baseline (p>0.3)\n- dt_embed_dim=0: mean eval 563, indistinguishable from trained (p=0.78)\n- Untrained: mean eval 600, -5% vs baseline\n\n**Cartpole Swingup (no CIVO):**\n- Baseline: mean eval 818, CV 3%\n- Trained dt-emb: NVE 0.88-1.10, mean eval 680, -10%\n- dt_embed_dim=0: mean eval 670, indistinguishable (p=0.85)\n\n**Hopper Hop (no CIVO):**\n- Baseline: 250; trained dt-emb: 210, NVE 1.05; no dt-emb: 205\n\n**Mechanistic Analysis:**\n- RSSM fidelity: Walker reward gap 2.78× vs Cheetah 1.35×\n- Embedding separation: Walker 0.01/1K steps vs Cheetah 0.004/1K steps\n- Actor entropy: divergence only in Walker collapsed configs\n- Value calibration: Walker +45% bias, skew 1.8 vs Cheetah +8% bias, skew 0.3\n\n**NVE Threshold Diagnostic:**\n- Walker-only AUROC: 1.0\n- Cross-env AUROC: 0.58 (sensitivity 0.40, specificity 1.0)\n\n**Intervention pilot:**\n- Uncertainty-gated truncation: eval 520 (-45% baseline), NVE 1.35, 65% truncation rate, effective horizon 5.2\n\n## Experiment Design Reference (from review_context.yaml)\n\nThe full experiment plan includes 20 experiments. The paper covers most of them. Key experiments from the plan that the paper addresses:\n- Walker Walk 008d multi-seed (plan_011) — covered (3 seeds in paper, plan had 3)\n- Walker Walk 008f multi-seed (plan_012) — covered (2 seeds)\n- Walker Walk 008e_v3 multi-seed (plan_014, plan_016) — covered (4 seeds)\n- Walker Walk 008a multi-seed (plan_013) — covered (3 seeds)\n- Cheetah baseline + trained/untrained/no-embed (plans 020-023) — covered\n- Cartpole baseline + trained/no-embed (plans 050-052) — covered\n- RSSM fidelity (plan_030) — covered\n- Actor entropy (plan_031) — covered\n- Embedding cosine (plan_033) — covered\n- NVE threshold analysis (plan_034) — covered\n- Frozen dt-emb (plan_015) — covered\n- 008e_v3 additional seeds (plan_016) — covered\n- Uncertainty-gated pilot (plan_060) — covered\n- Hopper Hop (plan_040) — covered\n- Full-SGS (018) — covered\n\nExperiments partially missing or under-reported:\n- Value prediction distribution (plan_032): mentioned in text (Section 4.6.4) but no table/figure — just reported as \"mean bias +45%, skew 1.8\" vs \"+8%, skew 0.3\"\n- Cartpole baseline seeds detail (plan_050): only summary table, no individual seed learning curves\n- Cheetah untrained dt_emb (plan_023): mentioned in Table 6 but minimal analysis\n- Hopper Hop: very sparse (only 1 paragraph, 1 table with 3 rows, no per-seed breakdown)\n\n## Your Task\n\nProvide a detailed review focusing on:\n\n1. **Experimental methodology**: Are the experiments well-designed? Do they support the claims? Are controls adequate?\n2. **Statistical rigor**: Sample sizes, significance testing, confidence intervals, effect sizes\n3. **Reproducibility**: Are details sufficient to reproduce?\n4. **Experiment coverage**: How well does the paper cover the planned experiments? Are missing experiments critical?\n5. **Causal claims**: Does the evidence support the causal claims made?\n6. **Specific weaknesses and strengths**\n\nStructure your review as:\n- Summary (2-3 sentences)\n- Strengths (bulleted)\n- Weaknesses (bulleted, numbered W1, W2, ...)\n- Questions for authors\n- Missing experiments or analyses\n- Overall score (1-6) with confidence (1-5)\n- Short justification for score\n","uuid":"c77b1e53-b862-4b6d-b787-656a0add8bb6","session_id":"2c57719a-f24e-4bf2-bbe7-05d690719237"}
