{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_019WxEfRZHc53FTnDvBnFrCd","type":"tool_result","content":"{\"result\":\"{\\\"success\\\": true, \\\"data\\\": {\\\"path\\\": \\\"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_9/projects/event-gated-adaptive-horizon/writing_plan.yaml\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"# Writing Plan — CoRL 2026\\\\n# Paper: Diagnostic Analysis of Temporal Abstraction in World-Model RL\\\\n# Deadline: 2026-05-29 (14 days from today)\\\\n# Format: 8 pages + references\\\\n# Last updated: 2026-05-15 (D041: supplementary diagnostics actor_loss sign flip + value_std growth rate; three post-CIVO outcomes from 009e oscillatory degradation; D040: C6 PARTIALLY FALSIFIED, multiple vulnerability pathways)\\\\n\\\\nvenue:\\\\n  name: CoRL 2026\\\\n  deadline: 2026-05-29\\\\n  format: \\\\\\\"8 pages + unlimited references\\\\\\\"\\\\n  template: corl2026  # IEEE two-column\\\\n  positioning: diagnostic-analysis  # NOT method paper\\\\n\\\\n# ============================================================\\\\n# PAPER STRUCTURE\\\\n# ============================================================\\\\n\\\\nsections:\\\\n  - id: abstract\\\\n    title: Abstract\\\\n    target_words: 200\\\\n    content_outline: |\\\\n      Temporal abstraction via variable-dt imagination in world-model RL (DreamerV3) consistently degrades performance.\\\\n      We conduct a factorial diagnostic isolating trained dt_embedding as the reliable trigger for pathological value\\\\n      overestimation (nve>1.5x, 4/4 separating power across seeds). Collapse is stochastic (seed-dependent), but the\\\\n      diagnostic marker is deterministic. Restricting imagination to dt=1 does not prevent collapse (1/2 seeds;\\\\n      008e_v3_s2 collapsed via non-CIVO pathway: eval-driven with increasing entropy, unlike 008d's value-driven\\\\n      CIVO). Baseline seed 2 stable — rules out seed fragility. Trained dt_embedding creates vulnerability\\\\n      through multiple pathways, not solely through the value overestimation feedback loop.\\\\n    claims_referenced: [C1, C2, C3, C6]\\\\n    data_ready: true\\\\n    writing_order: 8  # last\\\\n\\\\n  - id: introduction\\\\n    title: Introduction\\\\n    target_pages: 1.0\\\\n    content_outline: |\\\\n      (1) Temporal abstraction is a long-sought goal; world-model RL offers natural testbed via imagination dt.\\\\n      (2) Puzzle: all variable-rate attempts degrade. TAWM (Nhu et al., ICML 2025) shows Δt conditioning works\\\\n      in MPC (TD-MPC2) — why does it fail in imagination-based actor-critic? Novelty: dt-conditioning succeeds\\\\n      in MPC but fails in imagination — this paper identifies the architecture-specific vulnerability.\\\\n      (3) Contribution: strongly supported causal chain (trained dt_emb → conditioning-induced value overestimation\\\\n      (CIVO) — analogous to the delusional bias of Lu et al. (2018) but arising from model imprecision amplified\\\\n      by learned temporal conditioning, rather than policy-class constraints — nve>1.5x → stochastic collapse).\\\\n      Finding 6 (partially falsified): restricting imagination to dt=1 does not prevent collapse (1/2 seeds).\\\\n      Collapsed seed shows non-CIVO dynamics (eval-driven, entropy increasing); baseline s2 stable → rules\\\\n      out seed fragility. Trained dt_embedding creates vulnerability through multiple pathways.\\\\n      Diagnostic methodology with factorial design.\\\\n      (4) Scope: DreamerV3/RSSM, Walker Walk (+ cross-env if ready).\\\\n    claims_referenced: [C1, C2, C6]\\\\n    key_references: [hafner2023dreamerv3, nhu2025tawm, lu2018nondelusional, gumbsch2024thick]\\\\n    data_ready: true\\\\n    writing_order: 6\\\\n\\\\n  - id: related_work\\\\n    title: Related Work\\\\n    target_pages: 1.0\\\\n    content_outline: |\\\\n      (1) Temporal abstraction in RL: options (Sutton 1999), FiGAR, TempoRL, SDAR — all model-free.\\\\n      (2) World-model RL & imagination: DreamerV1-V3, IRIS, TWM — standard dt=1 imagination.\\\\n      DreamerV4 (Hafner & Yan 2025): transformer replaces RSSM — discuss whether CIVO mechanism transfers.\\\\n      (3) Variable-rate world models: TAWM (Nhu et al., ICML 2025, MPC setting, beneficial Δt conditioning —\\\\n      key contrast: succeeds in MPC but fails in imagination-based actor-critic), THICK (Gumbsch et al., ICLR 2024,\\\\n      hierarchical temporal abstraction in Dreamer), Hieros (Mattes et al., ICML 2024, hierarchical imagination),\\\\n      LS-Imagine (Li et al., ICLR 2025 Oral, goal-conditioned horizon extension), MTS3 (Shaj et al., NeurIPS 2023,\\\\n      multi-time-scale SSM), DreamSmooth (Lee et al., ICLR 2024, reward smoothing for world models).\\\\n      (4) Value overestimation in MBRL: MBPO, MOPO, delusional bias (Lu 2018 — explicitly differentiate:\\\\n      policy-class constraints vs our CIVO from model imprecision + learned conditioning), MAD-TD.\\\\n      Tallec et al. 2019: time-discretization invariance foundation.\\\\n      (5) Rollout quality: Frauenknecht et al. (ICLR 2025) — rollout divergence supports CIVO diagnosis.\\\\n      (6) Diagnostic methodology precedent: Implementation Matters, What Matters for Actor-Critic.\\\\n      Differentiate from TAWM (MPC vs imagination paradigm — opposite conclusions on Δt conditioning).\\\\n    claims_referenced: []\\\\n    key_references: [sutton1999options, sharma2017figar, biedenkapp2021temporl, hafner2023dreamerv3,\\\\n                     nhu2025tawm, gumbsch2024thick, mattes2024hieros, shaj2023mts3, li2025lsimagine,\\\\n                     janner2019mbpo, yu2020mopo, lu2018nondelusional, su2020conqur,\\\\n                     engstrom2020implementation, andrychowicz2021whatmatters, frauenknecht2025rollouts,\\\\n                     lee2024dreamsmooth, hafner2025dreamerv4, tallec2019making]\\\\n    data_ready: true\\\\n    writing_order: 7\\\\n\\\\n  - id: methodology\\\\n    title: \\\\\\\"Experimental Setup\\\\\\\"\\\\n    target_pages: 1.5\\\\n    content_outline: |\\\\n      (1) DreamerV3 base architecture (RSSM, symlog, discrete latents) — brief, cite original.\\\\n      (2) Variable-rate imagination mechanism: dt_embedding (trained/untrained/removed), temporal subsampling,\\\\n      imagination horizon H. How each factor modifies imagination rollouts.\\\\n      (3) Factorial design: 2×2×2 grid (dt_emb training × subsample × H) + fixed-dt baselines + mitigation.\\\\n      Present grid as table with cell assignments.\\\\n      (4) Diagnostic metrics: eval return, v/e ratio, normalized v/e (nve = exp_v/e / baseline_v/e at same step),\\\\n      nve>1.5x threshold, RSSM fidelity (obs_MSE, reward_MAE at dt=1 vs dt=2).\\\\n      Supplementary diagnostics (D041):\\\\n      - actor_loss sign flip: DreamerV3 actor_loss is normally negative; positive flip (+0.011@85K in 009e)\\\\n        directly signals value function misleading the actor — more targeted than nve for delusional critic damage.\\\\n      - value_std growth rate: exponential growth (5.7→17.4, doubling per 10K steps in 009e) captures\\\\n        oscillatory degradation that nve misses due to \\\\\\\"false recovery\\\\\\\" in oscillating value/eval trajectories.\\\\n      (5) Environment: Walker Walk (DMC), 500K baseline / 105K treatments, 2+ seeds per config.\\\\n    claims_referenced: [C1, C2, C3, C4, C5, C6]\\\\n    key_references: [hafner2023dreamerv3, agarwal2021precipice]\\\\n    data_ready: true\\\\n    writing_order: 2\\\\n\\\\n  - id: results\\\\n    title: Results\\\\n    target_pages: 2.5\\\\n    content_outline: |\\\\n      Organized by findings (F1-F6 mapping to C1-C6):\\\\n      F1 (C1): All dt>1 degrade — learning curves overlay (exp_001, 005, 006, 007).\\\\n      F2 (C2): Trained dt_emb → nve>1.5x (4/4 separation). 008d vs 008f causal control.\\\\n      Three post-CIVO outcomes from same trained dt_emb config (008d, 3 seeds):\\\\n      - 008d s0: full collapse (Pathway A — value explosion, eval decline, entropy ↓)\\\\n      - 009b s2: self-correction (transient nve>1.5x → value self-corrects, eval recovers to 268)\\\\n      - 009e s1: oscillatory degradation (actor permanently damaged — actor_loss flips positive +0.011@85K,\\\\n        value_std exponential growth 5.7→17.4, eval oscillates 82→205→113→174→121→185→103)\\\\n      Supplementary diagnostics: actor_loss sign flip more targeted than nve; value_std captures damage\\\\n      that nve misses during oscillatory \\\\\\\"false recovery\\\\\\\" phases.\\\\n      F3 (C3): Untrained dt_emb prevents drift — 008a@105K=778, nve 0.59-0.93x.\\\\n      F4 (C4): dt=2 > dt=4 monotonic degradation.\\\\n      F5 (C5): Horizon/subsample secondary — 008c (H=8) vs 008a (H=15).\\\\n      F6 (C6, partially falsified): dt=1 imagination does not prevent collapse (1/2 seeds).\\\\n      008e_v3 seed 1 healthy (869.9, 95% baseline), seed 2 collapsed (715→137, nve=3.78x).\\\\n      009a baseline s2 stable (618→596→836) — rules out seed fragility hypothesis.\\\\n      Key insight: 008e_v3_s2 collapse mechanism differs from classic CIVO (008d):\\\\n      008d = value explosion (+130%) → eval decline → entropy ↓ (classic CIVO);\\\\n      008e_v3_s2 = eval crash (-81%) → value stable → entropy ↑ (policy instability).\\\\n      Trained dt_embedding creates vulnerability through multiple pathways, not solely\\\\n      through the value overestimation feedback loop.\\\\n    claims_referenced: [C1, C2, C3, C4, C5, C6]\\\\n    experiments_required:\\\\n      - exp_001_baseline  # DONE\\\\n      - exp_005_event_gated_v4  # DONE\\\\n      - exp_006_fixed_dt2  # DONE\\\\n      - exp_007_fixed_dt4  # DONE\\\\n      - exp_008a_no_subsample_dt2  # DONE\\\\n      - exp_008c_no_subsample_dt2_h8  # DONE\\\\n      - exp_008d_subsample_on_h8  # DONE\\\\n      - exp_008e_v3_subsample_on_dt1_h15  # DONE (seed=1)\\\\n      - exp_008f_no_dt_embed_subsample_on_h8  # DONE\\\\n      - exp_009b_008d_walker_s2  # DONE\\\\n      - exp_009c_008f_walker_s2  # DONE\\\\n      - exp_008e_v3_walker_s1  # DONE (seed=1, deterministic reproduction of s0)\\\\n      - exp_008e_v3_walker_s2  # DONE (seed=2, COLLAPSED: 715→137, nve=3.78x)\\\\n      - exp_009a_baseline_walker_s2  # DONE (stable: 618→596→836 @85-105K)\\\\n      - exp_009e_008d_walker_s1  # DONE (oscillatory degradation: actor_loss +0.011@85K, value_std 5.7→17.4)\\\\n    data_ready: true  # D041: all key experiments complete (009d baseline s1 still RUNNING, not blocking)\\\\n    writing_order: 1  # write first — data-rich, anchors everything\\\\n\\\\n  - id: analysis\\\\n    title: \\\\\\\"Analysis & Discussion\\\\\\\"\\\\n    target_pages: 1.5\\\\n    content_outline: |\\\\n      (1) Mechanism: trained dt_emb enables reward head to produce systematically biased dt>1 predictions\\\\n      (reward gap 2.78x in 008d). Critic trained on these → optimistic value landscape → actor exploitation.\\\\n      RSSM fidelity table: absolute errors + ratios side-by-side.\\\\n      (2) Three post-CIVO outcomes (same config, 3 seeds): full collapse (008d s0), self-correction (009b s2),\\\\n      oscillatory degradation (009e s1). Why do seeds diverge? (plasticity, primacy bias).\\\\n      009e reveals actor_loss sign flip as direct delusional critic damage marker; value_std exponential\\\\n      growth as oscillatory degradation detector that nve misses. Connect to Zhang 2026, Lyle 2022, Bjorck 2022.\\\\n      (3) Why MPC is immune: TAWM uses Δt conditioning successfully because MPC re-plans from real states.\\\\n      Imagination-based training accumulates value error across full rollout → exploit.\\\\n      (4) 008f trade-off: removing dt_emb eliminates CIVO but destroys reward prediction (75x MAE).\\\\n      008e_v3 (partially falsified): dt=1 imagination — seed 1 healthy, seed 2 collapsed via non-CIVO\\\\n      pathway (eval-driven, entropy increasing vs 008d's value-driven, entropy decreasing). 009a baseline\\\\n      s2 stable → collapse is config-caused, not seed-specific. Trained dt_embedding creates vulnerability\\\\n      through multiple pathways, not solely through the value overestimation feedback loop.\\\\n      (7) Multiple vulnerability pathways: CIVO (value-driven, 008d) is one pathway; 008e_v3_s2 reveals\\\\n      a second pathway (eval-driven policy instability) that also requires trained dt_embedding but operates\\\\n      independently of imagination dt. This broadens the diagnostic beyond CIVO alone.\\\\n      (5) Implications: current RSSM insufficient for dt>1 imagination; hierarchy (THICK, Hieros) as correct direction.\\\\n      (6) DreamerV4 (Hafner & Yan 2025): transformer replaces RSSM — discuss whether CIVO mechanism transfers\\\\n      to transformer world models (RSSM-specific vs potentially broader vulnerability).\\\\n    claims_referenced: [C2, C3, C6]\\\\n    key_references: [nhu2025tawm, lu2018nondelusional, zhang2026instability, lyle2022capacity,\\\\n                     lee2024dreamsmooth, ma2024harmonydream, gumbsch2024thick, mattes2024hieros,\\\\n                     hafner2025dreamerv4, tallec2019making]\\\\n    data_ready: true\\\\n    writing_order: 3\\\\n\\\\n  - id: conclusion\\\\n    title: Conclusion\\\\n    target_pages: 0.5\\\\n    content_outline: |\\\\n      Summarize causal chain (C1-C5 solid). C6 (partially falsified): dt=1 imagination does not prevent\\\\n      collapse; trained dt_embedding creates vulnerability through multiple pathways (CIVO value-driven\\\\n      + non-CIVO eval-driven policy instability). Limitations: single environment (Walker Walk) primary,\\\\n      DreamerV3/RSSM-specific. Future: uncertainty-gated imagination truncation, hierarchical approaches,\\\\n      improved RSSM fidelity, characterizing the multiple failure pathways of temporal conditioning.\\\\n    claims_referenced: [C2, C6]\\\\n    data_ready: true\\\\n    writing_order: 9\\\\n\\\\n# ============================================================\\\\n# FIGURES\\\\n# ============================================================\\\\n\\\\nfigures:\\\\n  - id: fig1_learning_curves\\\\n    title: \\\\\\\"Learning curves across all configurations\\\\\\\"\\\\n    description: |\\\\n      Hero figure. All experiments overlaid showing systematic degradation pattern.\\\\n      Groups: baseline (dt=1), fixed dt>1 (006, 007), learned gate (005),\\\\n      factorial ablations (008a-f), mitigation (008e_v3).\\\\n    data_source: [exp_001_baseline, exp_005_event_gated_v4, exp_006_fixed_dt2, exp_007_fixed_dt4,\\\\n                  exp_008a_no_subsample_dt2, exp_008d_subsample_on_h8, exp_008e_v3_subsample_on_dt1_h15]\\\\n    placement: results (F1/C1)\\\\n    status: data_ready  # all experiments DONE\\\\n    gpu_cost: 0\\\\n\\\\n  - id: fig2_nve_trajectory\\\\n    title: \\\\\\\"Normalized value/eval ratio trajectories — diagnostic marker\\\\\\\"\\\\n    description: |\\\\n      Top panel: nve over training steps for key experiments. 1.5x threshold line marked.\\\\n      Show: 008d s0 (sustained >1.5x → full collapse), 009b s2 (transient >1.5x → self-correction),\\\\n      009e s1 (oscillatory — nve fluctuates, \\\\\\\"false recovery\\\\\\\"), 008f seeds (both <1.5x),\\\\n      008e_v3 s1 (healthy, ~0.80x), 008e_v3 s2 (nve=3.78x → non-CIVO collapse).\\\\n      4/4 trained-vs-untrained separation at threshold.\\\\n      Bottom panel (supplementary): actor_loss trajectory for 008d configs (3 seeds).\\\\n      009e actor_loss flips positive (+0.011@85K) — direct marker of delusional critic damage.\\\\n      008d s0 actor_loss also pathological; 009b s2 actor_loss remains negative (self-corrected).\\\\n    data_source: [exp_008d_subsample_on_h8, exp_009b_008d_walker_s2, exp_009e_008d_walker_s1,\\\\n                  exp_008f_no_dt_embed_subsample_on_h8, exp_009c_008f_walker_s2,\\\\n                  exp_008e_v3_subsample_on_dt1_h15, exp_001_baseline]\\\\n    placement: results (F2/C2)\\\\n    status: data_ready\\\\n    gpu_cost: 0\\\\n\\\\n  - id: fig3_factorial_grid\\\\n    title: \\\\\\\"Factorial experiment summary (2×2 grid)\\\\\\\"\\\\n    description: |\\\\n      2×2 grid: dt_emb (trained/untrained) × subsample (ON/OFF), with H as secondary axis.\\\\n      Each cell shows final eval return + nve status (healthy/pathological).\\\\n      Clearly shows trained dt_emb as the separating factor.\\\\n    data_source: [exp_008a_no_subsample_dt2, exp_008c_no_subsample_dt2_h8,\\\\n                  exp_008d_subsample_on_h8, exp_006_fixed_dt2]\\\\n    placement: results (F2-F5)\\\\n    status: data_ready\\\\n    gpu_cost: 0\\\\n\\\\n  - id: fig4_mechanism_diagram\\\\n    title: \\\\\\\"Causal mechanism diagram\\\\\\\"\\\\n    description: |\\\\n      Flow diagram: trained dt_embedding → RSSM dt>1 predictions (low fidelity) →\\\\n      reward head systematic bias (2.78x gap) → critic value overestimation (nve>1.5x) →\\\\n      actor exploits overestimated values → performance collapse (stochastic gate: sustained vs transient).\\\\n      008e_v3 (partially falsified): show second pathway — trained dt_embedding → non-CIVO policy\\\\n      instability (eval-driven, entropy ↑). Dashed arrow labeled \\\\\\\"Pathway B\\\\\\\" distinct from main CIVO\\\\n      \\\\\\\"Pathway A\\\\\\\". Both require trained dt_embedding; only Pathway A requires dt>1 imagination.\\\\n    data_source: []  # conceptual figure\\\\n    placement: analysis\\\\n    status: ready_to_draw\\\\n    gpu_cost: 0\\\\n\\\\n  - id: fig5_dt_amplification\\\\n    title: \\\\\\\"Performance vs dt (monotonic degradation)\\\\\\\"\\\\n    description: |\\\\n      Bar or line chart: dt=1 (baseline ~950) > dt=2 (peak 485) > dt=4 (peak 177).\\\\n      Clear monotonic relationship.\\\\n    data_source: [exp_001_baseline, exp_006_fixed_dt2, exp_007_fixed_dt4]\\\\n    placement: results (F4/C4)\\\\n    status: data_ready\\\\n    gpu_cost: 0\\\\n\\\\n  - id: fig6_multiple_pathways\\\\n    title: \\\\\\\"Multiple vulnerability pathways: CIVO vs non-CIVO collapse\\\\\\\"\\\\n    description: |\\\\n      Two-panel or annotated overlay showing contrasting collapse dynamics:\\\\n      Left/Top: 008d s1 classic CIVO (value explosion → eval decline → entropy ↓).\\\\n      Right/Bottom: 008e_v3 s2 non-CIVO (eval crash → value stable → entropy ↑).\\\\n      Both require trained dt_embedding. 009a baseline s2 stable (618→596→836) as control.\\\\n      Key message: trained dt_embedding creates vulnerability through multiple pathways.\\\\n    data_source: [exp_001_baseline, exp_008e_v3_subsample_on_dt1_h15,\\\\n                  exp_008e_v3_walker_s2, exp_008d_subsample_on_h8,\\\\n                  exp_009a_baseline_walker_s2]\\\\n    placement: results/analysis (F6/C6)\\\\n    status: data_ready  # D040: 009a baseline s2 confirms interpretation\\\\n    gpu_cost: 0\\\\n\\\\n# ============================================================\\\\n# TABLES\\\\n# ============================================================\\\\n\\\\ntables:\\\\n  - id: tab1_rssm_fidelity\\\\n    title: \\\\\\\"RSSM prediction fidelity at dt=1 vs dt=2\\\\\\\"\\\\n    description: |\\\\n      Three models (baseline, 008d collapsed, 008f no-dt-emb) × two metrics (obs_MSE, reward_MAE)\\\\n      × two dt values (1, 2). Report absolute values AND ratios. Key: 008d reward gap 2.78x\\\\n      (delusional source), 008f reward gap 1.01x (no distinction → no exploitation but also no learning).\\\\n    data_source: [exp_rssm_fidelity_analysis]\\\\n    placement: analysis\\\\n    status: data_ready\\\\n    gpu_cost: 0\\\\n\\\\n  - id: tab2_factorial_summary\\\\n    title: \\\\\\\"Factorial experiment design and results\\\\\\\"\\\\n    description: |\\\\n      Full grid showing all experimental conditions and key outcomes.\\\\n      Columns: exp_id, dt_emb (trained/untrained/none), subsample, H, dt_imag, final_eval,\\\\n      nve_peak, collapse_status.\\\\n    data_source: [all_experiments]\\\\n    placement: methodology/results\\\\n    status: data_ready\\\\n    gpu_cost: 0\\\\n\\\\n  - id: tab3_multi_seed\\\\n    title: \\\\\\\"Multi-seed results summary\\\\\\\"\\\\n    description: |\\\\n      Per-config seed results with IQM. Show 008d (3 seeds, 3 outcomes: collapse/self-correction/oscillatory),\\\\n      008f (0/2 collapse), baseline (0/2 collapse).\\\\n      [D041] 008d config now has 3 seeds with 3 distinct post-CIVO outcomes:\\\\n      - 008d s0: full collapse (eval 167→83, value explosion +130%)\\\\n      - 009b s2: self-correction (nve 2.05x→0.38x, eval 141→268)\\\\n      - 009e s1: oscillatory degradation (actor_loss flips +0.011@85K, value_std 5.7→17.4,\\\\n        eval oscillates 82→205→113→174→121→185→103)\\\\n      008e_v3: seed 1 healthy (869.9), seed 2 COLLAPSED via non-CIVO pathway (715→137, nve=3.78x).\\\\n      009a baseline s2 stable (836@105K).\\\\n      [D041] 009d (baseline s1 repeat) still RUNNING — add when done, not blocking.\\\\n    data_source: [exp_008d_subsample_on_h8, exp_009b_008d_walker_s2,\\\\n                  exp_008f_no_dt_embed_subsample_on_h8, exp_009c_008f_walker_s2,\\\\n                  exp_008e_v3_subsample_on_dt1_h15, exp_008e_v3_walker_s2,\\\\n                  exp_001_baseline, exp_009a_baseline_walker_s2]\\\\n    placement: results\\\\n    status: data_ready  # D040: core seeds complete; 009d/009e supplementary\\\\n    gpu_cost: 0\\\\n\\\\n# ============================================================\\\\n# WRITING ORDER (by dependency)\\\\n# ============================================================\\\\n\\\\nwriting_order:\\\\n  - order: 1\\\\n    section: results\\\\n    reason: \\\\\\\"Data-rich, anchors all other sections. Most figures/tables go here.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    blocker: null\\\\n\\\\n  - order: 2\\\\n    section: methodology\\\\n    reason: \\\\\\\"Defines experiment design referenced by results. Can write in parallel with results.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    blocker: null\\\\n\\\\n  - order: 3\\\\n    section: analysis\\\\n    reason: \\\\\\\"Interprets results, requires results section to be stable.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    blocker: results\\\\n\\\\n  - order: 4\\\\n    section: related_work\\\\n    reason: \\\\\\\"literature_map complete (72 papers). Position against TAWM, THICK, Hieros.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    blocker: null  # can write early\\\\n\\\\n  - order: 5\\\\n    section: introduction\\\\n    reason: \\\\\\\"Frames contributions — needs results and analysis solidified.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    blocker: [results, analysis]\\\\n\\\\n  - order: 6\\\\n    section: conclusion\\\\n    reason: \\\\\\\"Summarizes; last content section.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    blocker: [results, analysis]\\\\n\\\\n  - order: 7\\\\n    section: abstract\\\\n    reason: \\\\\\\"Written last, distills entire paper.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    blocker: [introduction, results, analysis, conclusion]\\\\n\\\\n# ============================================================\\\\n# LITERATURE STRATEGY\\\\n# ============================================================\\\\n\\\\nliterature:\\\\n  must_cite:\\\\n    - hafner2023dreamerv3  # base system\\\\n    - hafner2020dreamerv1  # architecture family\\\\n    - hafner2021dreamerv2  # discrete latents predecessor\\\\n    - sutton1999options  # temporal abstraction foundation\\\\n    - lu2018nondelusional  # delusional bias theory\\\\n    - nhu2025tawm  # closest competitor — MUST differentiate MPC vs imagination\\\\n    - gumbsch2024thick  # hierarchical alternative in Dreamer\\\\n    - mattes2024hieros  # hierarchical imagination\\\\n    - janner2019mbpo  # model exploitation in MBRL\\\\n    - agarwal2021precipice  # evaluation methodology (IQM)\\\\n    - henderson2018deep  # seed variance\\\\n    - frauenknecht2025rollouts  # imagination rollout quality (ICLR 2025)\\\\n    - lee2024dreamsmooth  # reward prediction bottleneck\\\\n    - zhang2026instability  # training instability dynamics\\\\n\\\\n  should_cite:\\\\n    - li2025lsimagine  # concurrent Dreamer horizon extension\\\\n    - shaj2023mts3  # multi-rate dynamics foundation\\\\n    - sharma2017figar  # FiGAR — learned action repeat\\\\n    - biedenkapp2021temporl  # TempoRL — model-free temporal abstraction\\\\n    - fujimoto2018td3  # overestimation in actor-critic\\\\n    - vanhasselt2016double  # double Q-learning\\\\n    - yu2020mopo  # pessimistic MBRL\\\\n    - su2020conqur  # delusional bias mitigation\\\\n    - tallec2019making  # time discretization sensitivity\\\\n    - engstrom2020implementation  # diagnostic methodology precedent\\\\n    - andrychowicz2021whatmatters  # factorial study precedent\\\\n    - lyle2022capacity  # necessary vs sufficient conditions\\\\n    - bjorck2022variance  # early outlier runs\\\\n    - qiao2023mind  # primacy bias in MBRL\\\\n    - ma2024harmonydream  # obs vs reward prediction balance\\\\n    - voelcker2025madtd  # value misgeneralization\\\\n    - hafner2025dreamerv4  # DreamerV4 (scope limitation discussion)\\\\n\\\\n  consider_citing:\\\\n    - zhang2026hwm  # hierarchical world model planning\\\\n    - park2021sar  # time-discretization invariant action repeat\\\\n    - nikishin2022primacy  # primacy bias\\\\n    - sokar2023dormant  # dormant neurons\\\\n    - lyle2024normalization  # normalization & effective LR\\\\n    - kumar2022dr3  # feature aliasing\\\\n    - hansen2024tdmpc2  # TD-MPC2 (contrast MPC paradigm)\\\\n    - hafner2022director  # hierarchical Dreamer\\\\n\\\\n# ============================================================\\\\n# RISK ASSESSMENT\\\\n# ============================================================\\\\n\\\\nrisks:\\\\n  - id: risk_cross_env\\\\n    severity: medium\\\\n    description: \\\\\\\"Cheetah Run / Cartpole experiments still QUEUED (exp_010a). No cross-environment data.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    mitigation: \\\\\\\"Scope claims to Walker Walk + DreamerV3. Discuss generalizability as future work. If 010a finishes by May 27, include.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    dependent_claims: [C1]\\\\n    blocking_experiments: [exp_010a_cheetah_baseline_s1]\\\\n\\\\n  - id: risk_c6_seed2\\\\n    severity: resolved  # D040: C6 PARTIALLY FALSIFIED — 009a baseline s2 stable, interpretation complete\\\\n    description: |\\\\n      [D040] C6 PARTIALLY FALSIFIED. 009a baseline s2 stable (618→596→836) — rules out seed fragility.\\\\n      008e_v3_s2 collapse confirmed config-caused but via non-CIVO pathway (eval-driven, entropy ↑).\\\\n      Trained dt_embedding creates vulnerability through multiple pathways:\\\\n      Pathway A (CIVO): value-driven, entropy ↓ (008d pattern)\\\\n      Pathway B (non-CIVO): eval-driven policy instability, entropy ↑ (008e_v3_s2 pattern)\\\\n      dt=1 imagination eliminates Pathway A but not Pathway B.\\\\n    mitigation: \\\\\\\"C6 reframed as 'partially falsified' with dual-pathway insight. No longer blocking — interpretation complete.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    dependent_claims: [C6]\\\\n    blocking_experiments: []  # resolved\\\\n\\\\n  - id: risk_baseline_s2\\\\n    severity: resolved  # D040: 009a DONE\\\\n    description: \\\\\\\"exp_009a_baseline_walker_s2 DONE. Stable at 85-105K (618→596→836). Confirms seed 2 not inherently fragile.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    mitigation: \\\\\\\"Two-seed baseline available (s0: 915.67, s2: 836@105K).\\\\\\\"\\\\n    dependent_claims: [C1, C2, C3]\\\\n    blocking_experiments: []  # resolved\\\\n\\\\n  - id: risk_collapse_probability\\\\n    severity: resolved  # D041: 009e DONE — reveals third outcome (oscillatory degradation)\\\\n    description: |\\\\n      [D041] 009e (008d seed 1 repeat) DONE: oscillatory degradation — neither full collapse nor\\\\n      self-correction. actor_loss flips positive (+0.011@85K), value_std exponential growth (5.7→17.4).\\\\n      3 seeds of 008d config now show 3 distinct post-CIVO outcomes: full collapse / self-correction /\\\\n      oscillatory degradation. This strengthens \\\\\\\"systemic vulnerability\\\\\\\" narrative — trained dt_embedding\\\\n      causes pathological behavior in 2/3 seeds (only 009b self-corrects).\\\\n    mitigation: \\\\\\\"Report 3 post-CIVO outcomes transparently. Actor_loss sign flip and value_std as supplementary diagnostics.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    dependent_claims: [C2]\\\\n    blocking_experiments: []  # resolved\\\\n\\\\n  - id: risk_page_budget\\\\n    severity: medium\\\\n    description: \\\\\\\"8 pages tight for 6 claims + factorial design + RSSM analysis + multi-seed.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    mitigation: \\\\\\\"Prioritize C1, C2, C6 in main text. C3-C5 can be condensed. Use appendix for extended data.\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n# ============================================================\\\\n# TIMELINE\\\\n# ============================================================\\\\n\\\\ntimeline:\\\\n  - date: 2026-05-15\\\\n    milestone: \\\\\\\"Writing plan finalized. Begin Results + Methodology drafting.\\\\\\\"\\\\n  - date: 2026-05-17\\\\n    milestone: \\\\\\\"Results draft complete. All figures generated (0 GPU cost).\\\\\\\"\\\\n  - date: 2026-05-19\\\\n    milestone: \\\\\\\"Analysis & Discussion draft. Related Work draft.\\\\\\\"\\\\n  - date: 2026-05-21\\\\n    milestone: \\\\\\\"Introduction draft. Full paper skeleton assembled.\\\\\\\"\\\\n  - date: 2026-05-23\\\\n    milestone: \\\\\\\"Internal review pass. Abstract + Conclusion. Page budget check.\\\\\\\"\\\\n  - date: 2026-05-25\\\\n    milestone: \\\\\\\"Revision pass. Incorporate any new experiment results (RUNNING → DONE).\\\\\\\"\\\\n  - date: 2026-05-27\\\\n    milestone: \\\\\\\"Final polish. Reference check. Supplementary materials.\\\\\\\"\\\\n  - date: 2026-05-29\\\\n    milestone: \\\\\\\"Submission deadline.\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\", \\\"total_chars\\\": 26607, \\\"truncated\\\": false}, \\\"error\\\": null, \\\"metadata\\\": {}}\"}"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01FXrjvQWSFc6K3k2oYyLyeD","session_id":"2c57719a-f24e-4bf2-bbe7-05d690719237","uuid":"da65cc6f-1a6f-4863-9c44-badd73cf0507","timestamp":"2026-05-16T13:02:40.015Z"}
