N (3 seeds)\n563\t  plan_id: plan_022\n564\t  description: Cross-environment causal control — removing dt_embedding in Cheetah\n565\t  expected_results:\n566\t    seed1_nve_peak: 1.1\n567\t    seed1_eval_105K: 420\n568\t    seed2_nve_peak: 0.95\n569\t    seed2_eval_105K: 380\n570\t    seed3_nve_peak: 1.18\n571\t    seed3_eval_105K: 350\n572\t    nve_above_1.5x_count: 0/3\n573\t    collapse_count: 0/3\n574\t    mean_eval_105K: 383\n575\t    vs_baseline_degradation: 54%\n576\t    reward_MAE_vs_baseline: 60x\n577\t  result_rationale: 'Without dt_embedding, the CIVO mechanism is structurally blocked\n578\t    — the critic has no channel to condition on dt and therefore cannot develop systematic\n579\t    overestimation for dt>1 trajectories. All 3 seeds staying below nve=1.5x extends\n580\t    the 4/4 Walker separation to 7/7 across environments (trained 5/5 exceed, untrained/absent\n581\t    0/7 exceed). Performance degradation (~54% vs baseline) is expected because removing\n582\t    dt_embedding impairs reward prediction quality (same mechanism as Walker 008f:\n583\t    reward head cannot distinguish dt=1/dt=2 transitions), but critically there is\n584\t    NO collapse. The degradation is stable and bounded.'\n585\t  tables:\n586\t  - title: Cheetah Run no-dt_emb NVE confirmation\n587\t    columns:\n588\t    - step\n589\t    - s1_nve\n590\t    - s2_nve\n591\t    - s3_nve\n592\t    - mean_eval\n593\t    rows:\n594\t    - - 25000\n595\t      - 1.1\n596\t      - 0.95\n597\t      - 1.05\n598\t      - 190\n599\t    - - 45000\n600\t      - 0.8\n601\t      - 0.75\n602\t      - 0.82\n603\t      - 280\n604\t    - - 65000\n605\t      - 0.6\n606\t      - 0.55\n607\t      - 0.65\n608\t      - 340\n609\t    - - 85000\n610\t      - 0.5\n611\t      - 0.48\n612\t      - 0.55\n613\t      - 370\n614\t    - - 105000\n615\t      - 0.45\n616\t      - 0.42\n617\t      - 0.5\n618\t      - 383\n619\t  figures_description:\n620\t  - 'NVE band plot: all three seeds declining below 1.0x, converging toward 0.4-0.5x\n621\t    by 105K. 1.5x threshold line never approached.'\n622\t  analysis: 'Cross-environment causal control confirmed. The 1.5x threshold achieves\n623\t    perfect separation: 5/5 trained dt_emb seeds exceed it, 0/5 absent dt_emb seeds\n624\t    approach it. This 10/10 classification accuracy across Walker+Cheetah exceeds\n625\t    the ≥90% hypothesis requirement.'\n626\t- name: Cheetah Run untrained dt_emb + no subsample (3 seeds)\n627\t  plan_id: plan_023\n628\t  description: Cross-environment value suppression with uninformative dt conditioning\n629\t  expected_results:\n630\t    seed1_nve_range:\n631\t    - 0.55\n632\t    - 0.88\n633\t    seed1_eval_105K: 620\n634\t    seed2_nve_range:\n635\t    - 0.5\n636\t    - 0.92\n637\t    seed2_eval_105K: 580\n638\t    seed3_nve_range:\n639\t    - 0.52\n640\t    - 0.85\n641\t    seed3_eval_105K: 640\n642\t    mean_eval_105K: 613\n643\t    vs_baseline: -26%\n644\t    nve_always_below_1x: true\n645\t    zigzag_recovery_pattern: true\n646\t  result_rationale: Untrained dt_embedding in Cheetah Run should replicate Walker\n647\t    008a's value suppression pattern. The uninformative random embedding prevents\n648\t    the critic from learning dt-dependent value estimates, blocking both Pathway A\n649\t    and B. Performance (~75% baseline) is better than dt_embed_dim=0 (~46% baseline)\n650\t    because the untrained embedding still provides a consistent conditioning signal\n651\t    that aids representation learning, even though it conveys no temporal information.\n652\t    The zigzag recovery pattern reflects the agent periodically finding good policies\n653\t    through exploration but lacking the value calibration to maintain them stably.\n654\t  tables:\n655\t  - title: Cheetah Run untrained dt_emb value suppression\n656\t    columns:\n657\t    - step\n658\t    - mean_nve\n659\t    - mean_eval\n660\t    - baseline_eval\n661\t    rows:\n662\t    - - 55000\n663\t      - 0.85\n664\t      - 380\n665\t      - 447\n666\t    - - 65000\n667\t      - 0.7\n668\t      - 450\n669\t      - 520\n670\t    - - 75000\n671\t      - 0.72\n672\t      - 480\n673\t      - 600\n674\t    - - 85000\n675\t      - 0.65\n676\t      - 540\n677\t      - 660\n678\t    - - 95000\n679\t      - 0.6\n680\t      - 580\n681\t      - 720\n682\t    - - 105000\n683\t      - 0.55\n684\t      - 613\n685\t      - 650\n686\t  figures_description:\n687\t  - 'Three-seed band plot: NVE envelope 0.50-0.92x, consistently below 1.0x. Eval\n688\t    shows gradual ascent with zigzag variance.'\n689\t  analysis: Cross-environment replication of C3 (value growth suppression). The untrained\n690\t    dt_embedding is a structural blocker to CIVO independent of environment dynamics.\n691\t    Combined with Walker 008a (0.59-0.93x range), we have 4 seeds across 2 environments\n692\t    all showing NVE<1.0x throughout.\n693\t- name: 'RSSM prediction quality: dt=1 vs dt=2 transitions'\n694\t  plan_id: plan_030\n695\t  description: Quantify RSSM fidelity gap at dt=2 vs dt=1 in Cheetah Run models\n696\t  expected_results:\n697\t    cheetah_baseline_dt1_obs_MSE: 11.2\n698\t    cheetah_baseline_dt2_obs_MSE: 28.8\n699\t    cheetah_baseline_obs_gap: 2.57"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01FXrjvQWSFc6K3k2oYyLyeD","session_id":"2c57719a-f24e-4bf2-bbe7-05d690719237","uuid":"b142c555-6338-42c4-8710-9c6be2808edc","timestamp":"2026-05-16T13:03:16.102Z"}
